  <ym-title|Actual all-spectator equation comparison \V draft
  evidence><label|actual-all-spectator-equation-comparison--draft-evidence>

  Parent-authored under #26, session <verbatim|hairer-codex-existence-20261111>,
  claim through 2026-11-12 16:40 UTC. Lean pin
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Text:
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-equation-kernel-relay.tex>.
  Unintegrated candidate, independent review pending.

  <section|Scope><label|scope>

  The mark/erase part of Scotia.relay: same terminal portfolio calibration P,
  inverse bound, actual oriented matter errors, centered-to-all-tiling
  comparison, subpower varying coefficients, exact all-spectator zeros and
  calibrated catalog rows. Reuses existing calibration/invitation/census
  proofs and the finite-rank projection endpoint. Does not claim the
  thyme/lofty insertion/derivative vet clauses of full Scotia.relay. These
  are the next bounded relay obligation. The mathematical section retains the
  same selected funded family and all purchased local hypotheses; it does not
  construct a new history from generic local sections.

  <section|Source correspondence (all at pinned
  revision)><label|source-correspondence-all-at-pinned-revision>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.{Braze,matter,Hearth,solaris}> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Canopy.lean> (full read): eventually N, all
    p; one E/P/U with P=decor, inverse coeffSize\<less\>=2, all opened lower
    m/k and all motions; E=4(1+columns)*sphere+exp((supportExponent+2)*81)<em|storms>zeta/u;
    all its factors have Slow bounds. Manuscript uses preceding canonical
    marked-portfolio proof for that exact scalar bound and near-identity
    lemma.

    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.inviting> in
    <verbatim|MergeProof/Parterre.lean> (full read): actual section/stencil
    union, Credit, u\<gtr\>0,zeta\<gtr\>=0, terminal Keeper, regional cover
    \<less\>=81, cardinal<em|forcedAllowance\<less\>=1, sqrt
    allowance>storms\<less\>=1; one Cream with Z.x=e_j. Reused canonical
    terminal invitation, not replaced by bare P closeness.

    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.figment> in
    <verbatim|MergeProof/Figment.lean> (full read): actual Scrim.costs Music,
    same doors/Carol/Brine, finite census, exact coefficient and root
    estimates, gamma=1/8. Canonical actual-marked-portfolio-calibration
    contains this proof; selected-history attachment identifies its
    witnesses.

    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.{decor,sliver,chipcost,cheaper,notationL,signed_intro}>
    in <verbatim|MergeProof/Marimba.lean> (full read): inverse2 and
    normalized sections; <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Motion.{chips,repaint,modal,repainted_H,repainted_star,
    repaint_same,field_same}> in <verbatim|Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/Rebase.lean>
    (read through field_same). Chips are genuinely complex-linear even for
    conjugating motion: scalar is conjugated after the inverse patch. This
    convention is retained, rather than treating the semilinear action as
    complex-linear.

    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.{hallmarks,region,embark}> in
    <verbatim|MergeProof/Canyon.lean> (full read): finite oriented Q and Slow
    chip coefficients; rotates then gather_close before exact gathered
    identity, same terminal map and P.

    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.rotates> in
    <verbatim|MergeProof/Dollars.lean> (full read): fixed opening chosen
    after requested lower depth; cider constant times Slow E; gamma1/8
    absorbs to1/16; stencil fit. <verbatim|served_dollar> read for upcoming
    vet clause but not claimed in this draft.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Push.RelayDifference.{CenterRents,CenterRents.every,CenterRents.rents,
    center_price,corner_root,offset}> in <verbatim|Push/RELAY_DIFFERENCE/Placement.lean>:
    targeted reading from centered orientation to offset and every; same
    signed/conjugated copy orbit, injective fine-cell planting, 16-corner
    finite maximum principle, 3J*a_k \<less\>=a_m, either seam, literal
    spatial translate. Canonical centered-estimates proves the same
    planting/maximum principle; new prose applies it to the cutoff-dependent
    but fixed-stencil comparison functions.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Push.RelayDifference.{gathered,gather_close,gather_silent}>
    in <verbatim|Push/RELAY_DIFFERENCE/Combination.lean> (full read): every
    common tiling before root triangle; finite Slow coefficient sum; rate1/16
    to1/32; same finite Wilson denominator. Cannot intersect unrelated
    cofinal depth sets and conclude a common tiling.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Push.RelayDifference.{flight,Slow,Slow.sink,dollar_slow}>
    in <verbatim|Push/RELAY_DIFFERENCE/Rates.lean> (targeted): flight
    exp(epsilon*S.scale N); ordered filter; norm-based subpower, not
    boundedness of uncalibrated row. <verbatim|YM.Bid.{dollar,close,sober,exactOnSep,RelayBin}>
    in <verbatim|Bid/Drops.lean> read.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Push.Mark.skyprobes>, private
    <verbatim|radius_uniform,covers_radius, featured_partition> in
    <verbatim|MergeProof/SkyProbe.lean> (full read): finite basis of equation
    ideal makes MicroAt radius/period uniform in equation vector; finite
    spectator grades bound stencils, a_N*(s+m)\<less\>delta; spectator
    product continuous, bounded and LocalOn Outer; nonzero beta; exact
    terminal inverse cancels the tied threshold before a_N^(-d) scalar.

    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.{Astar,bindP,catalog,catalog_symm,marshal}>
    in <verbatim|MergeProof/Chaletbin.lean> (full read): B=X P X^-1 embedTo,
    moving ideal catalog; inverse-calibrate x as P^-1 X^-1 x; dollar implies
    Slow; resulting original carrier identity supplies exactOnSep; embark
    supplies Bid.close.

    <item><verbatim|YM.MergeProof.{Scotia,reception}> in
    <verbatim|MergeProof/Eureka.lean> (full read): constructs affordable
    uniformly bounded projection family via potage, catalog_symm and exact
    catalog kernel; invokes marshal for relay.mark. <verbatim|thyme,lofty>
    are other fields, not supplied by the mark argument.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Reuse and checks><label|reuse-and-checks>

  Canonical units read: marked-campaign-producer;
  marked-portfolio-calibration; actual-marked-portfolio-calibration;
  original-history-portfolio-attachment; finite-rank-kernel-transport;
  centered-estimates; targeted ope-filtration. No new literature theorem or
  free equation-ideal computation is claimed. The new argument is the exact
  same-data join plus all-spectator locality and quantitative finite
  combination. Shared background index searched earlier for
  rank/kernel/projection work; no additional external result needed.

  Commands run: targeted rg/cat/sed on those sources and canonical files;
  <verbatim|git diff --check> passed after TeX draft. No Lean source edits,
  new Lean build, axiom replay, TeX build or rendering for this candidate.
  Metadata remains draft. Review should verify every use of the same P and
  terminal normalization, actual scope of all opened/motion estimates, and no
  concealed production of Fridge/Scrim/Cream or the yet-separate vet clauses.

  Independent-review repair: read <verbatim|YM.Extraction.Lease.take/alive>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Lane/Lease.lean> in full. Added the actual
  root-rents-to-spectator bound before using the canonical D02 step-integral
  argument: common centered spectator budget, J=8(n+1), finer side
  with3J*a_j\<less\>=a_k, one shifted tiling, distinct cells,
  inverse-oriented tokens and planted inequality. Explicit normalizations now
  display V_N(v)=a_N^-d V.places(S_theta^-1 v), and embedTo=X S_theta coords
  R. Opening retains the same local period-uniform
  reserve/Cream/response/census inputs and centered observable bound. The
  finite-rank-kernel-transport text now cross-refers to this spectator step;
  its previous abbreviated root-to-smeared implication needed that addition.

